      "writtenOn": "2026-11-13T10:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A switch connect/auth failure returns [] (SSHHelper failure in the base `_discover_from_tables`, plus the dispatcher\u0027s `except -\u003e []`), so this path logs \"No hosts discovered\" and returns 0. For automation a failed query is indistinguishable from an empty switch, and `--apply` silently no-ops. Consider a nonzero exit (or a distinct \"could not query switch\" message) when the SSH query itself failed, vs an actually-empty result.",
      "revId": "40ed732b713bf26f0b3f602888bf2ba8ba397072",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
