      "writtenOn": "2026-11-13T10:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`existing_by_mac` is built once and not refreshed in the loop, and the create path doesn\u0027t check whether the chosen `name` already exists on the host. Two edges create duplicates: (1) a NIC swap where the new MAC lands on the port whose LLDP port-id is still `em1`, so the MAC match misses and a second `em1` is created; (2) the same MAC learned on two ports in one scan (mac-flap / active-backup / MLAG), created twice. The server enforces no name/MAC uniqueness, delete_interface matches by name, and modify indexes VLANs by sorted-name position, so a duplicate name affects later ops. This is the edge the idempotency NOTE (README ~612) doesn\u0027t cover. Tracking created names/MACs in a set and skip+warn on collision would close it.",
      "revId": "40ed732b713bf26f0b3f602888bf2ba8ba397072",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
