      "side": 1,
      "message": "The guard rejects colon-form MACs in the LLDP port-id, but EOS can advertise a dotted MAC as the neighbor port id (e.g. `7072.cfb7.6872` from a host without lldpd), and that string would become the interface name. Worth treating a dotted six-byte MAC as no usable name and falling back to `nicN` as well.",
      "revId": "40ed732b713bf26f0b3f602888bf2ba8ba397072",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
