      "side": 1,
      "message": "`_parse_fdb` strips the logical unit (`port.split(\".\")[0]` below) so its keys are physical (`ge-0/0/0`), but this line keys neighbors on the raw `tokens[0]`. On Junos that prints the Local Interface with the unit in `show lldp neighbors` (non-ELS EX2200/3300/4200; ELS QFX/EX4300 print without it), the LLDP keys (`ge-0/0/47.0`) never match the FDB keys (`ge-0/0/47`), so every row comes back neighbor\u003dNone and `--apply` matches nothing. The ELS-shaped test fixture is the one case that happens to join, so the suite doesn\u0027t catch it. `neighbors[tokens[0].split(\".\")[0]] \u003d {...}` aligns the key with the physical switch_port.",
      "revId": "40ed732b713bf26f0b3f602888bf2ba8ba397072",
